#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/seeds/the-henchmen/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Henchmen"
msgstr "Die Handlanger:innen"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-henchmen/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "> A group of mercenaries, bodyguards and defense contractors are hired by a billionaire to protect him in his remote stronghold after the great market collapse. Their boss eventually grew bored and ordered them to harass people from neighboring villages, barely making ends meet. He didn’t expect the bodyguards to turn on him. Now, after their boss had an unfortunate accident, these security personnel, with no experience in community building or with the local language, are trying to open up the stronghold and join their distrusting neighbors.\n"
msgstr ""
"> Nach dem großen Börsencrash wird eine Gruppe von Söldner:innen, Sicherheitspersonal und Bodyguards von einem Milliardär beauftragt, ihn in seiner abgelegenen Festung zu beschützen.\n"
"> Ihrem Boss wird irgendwann langweilig und er befiehlt ihnen Leute aus den benachbarten Dörfern zu behelligen, die gerade so über die runden kommen.\n"
"> Er hat nicht damit gerechnet, dass seine Bodyguards sich gegen ihn wenden.\n"
"> Jetzt, da ihr Boss einen unglücklichen Unfall hatte, versucht dieses Sicherheitspersonal ohne Erfahrung im Aufbau von Gemeinschaften oder Kenntnis über die örtliche Sprache, die Festung für alle zu öffnen, und sich ihren misstrauischen Nachbar:innen anzuschließen.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-henchmen/index.en.md
msgid "[Solarpunk Prompts Podcast Episode](https://podcast.tomasino.org/@SolarpunkPrompts/episodes/the-henchmen)"
msgstr "[Solarpunk Prompts Podcast Episode](https://podcast.tomasino.org/@SolarpunkPrompts/episodes/the-henchmen)"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-henchmen/index.en.md
msgid "[Transcript](https://wiki.tomasino.org/writing/Solarpunk-Prompts---The-Henchmen)"
msgstr "[Transkription](https://wiki.tomasino.org/writing/Solarpunk-Prompts---The-Henchmen)"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/seeds/the-miners/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Miners"
msgstr "Die Minenarbeiter:innen"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-miners/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "> A powerful co-op of rare earth miners, who long ago fought their owners and won, now face a new challenge: how to avoid becoming like them, knowing that without their work very few people will be able to produce electronics.\n"
msgstr "> Eine starke Genossenschaft von Minenarbeiter:innen für Seltene Erden, die lange gegen ihre Eigentümer:innen gekämpft haben, hat gewonnen und steht jetzt vor einer neuen Herausforderung: nicht so zu werden wie ihre alten Gegner:innen. Denn sie wissen, dass ohne ihre Arbeit kaum jemand Elektronikteile herstellen kann.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-miners/index.en.md
msgid "[Solarpunk Prompts Podcast Episode](https://podcast.tomasino.org/@SolarpunkPrompts/episodes/the-miners)"
msgstr "[Solarpunk Prompts Podcast Episode](https://podcast.tomasino.org/@SolarpunkPrompts/episodes/the-miners)"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-miners/index.en.md
msgid "[Transcript](https://wiki.tomasino.org/writing/Solarpunk-Prompts---The-Miners)"
msgstr "[Transkription](https://wiki.tomasino.org/writing/Solarpunk-Prompts---The-Miners)"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/seeds/the-moonshot/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Moonshot"
msgstr "Die Mondmission"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-moonshot/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "> A group of scientists, environmentalists, and politicians, such as lobbyists to the UN, are analyzing the footprints of the solar panels and windmills around the world, trying to answer the question: is sending a rocket to the moon and back to get a tonne of moon soil the best thing we can do in the middle of a climate crisis? Is moon helium fusion the best way forward?\n"
msgstr "> Eine Gruppe Wissenschaftler:innen, Ökolog:innen und Politiker:innen, wie Lobbyist:innen für die UN, analysieren den Fußabdruck von Solarkollektoren und Windkraftwerke überall auf der Welt. Sie versuchen die Frage zu beantworten: Ist eine Rakete zum Mond und zurück zu senden, um eine Tonne Mondgestein zu holen, wirklich das beste, das wir inmitten einer Klimakrise tun können? Ist Kernfusion mit Mondhelium die klügste Vorgehensweise?\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-moonshot/index.en.md
msgid "[Solarpunk Prompts Podcast Episode](https://podcast.tomasino.org/@SolarpunkPrompts/episodes/the-moonshot)"
msgstr "[Solarpunk Prompts Podcast Episode](https://podcast.tomasino.org/@SolarpunkPrompts/episodes/the-moonshot)"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-moonshot/index.en.md
msgid "[Transcript](https://wiki.tomasino.org/writing/Solarpunk-Prompts---The-Moonshot)"
msgstr "[Transkription](https://wiki.tomasino.org/writing/Solarpunk-Prompts---The-Moonshot)"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/seeds/the-non-economists/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Non-Economists"
msgstr "Die Nicht-Ökonomen"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-non-economists/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "> A small team of researchers is woken up by their notification inboxes exploding: their mundane and unexciting report might have just started an economic war between multiple regions and communities. In a world with tightly-controlled carbon budgets, the production, use and recycling of every product is a subject of LCA, or a LifeCycle Assessment. A bad result might change the design, or move the production to another region, with potential political consequences. How will the researchers deal with their newly acquired (in)fame? Will they trust their analysis, buckle under pressure, or decide to play politics?\n"
msgstr "> Ein kleines Team von Wissenschaftler:innen wird von ihren Benachrichtigungen aus dem Schlaf gerissen: ihre langweiligen und unaufgeregten Berichte könnten gerade einen Wirtschaftskrieg zwischen mehreren Regionen und Gemeinschaften ausgelöst haben. In einer Welt voller streng kontrollierter CO2-Budgets, unterläuft die Produktion, Verwendung und Recycling von jedem Produkt ein LCA, ein LfieCycle Assessment. Ein schlechtes Ergebnis könnte eine Designänderung bedeuten, oder die Produktion in eine andere Region verlegen, mit allen politischen Konsequenzen. Wie werden die Wissenschaftler:innen ihrem neuerworbenen Ruhm umgehen? Werden sie ihren Analysen vertrauen, oder geben sie dem Druck nach, oder politische Spielchen treiben?\n"

#. type: Title ##
#: content/seeds/the-non-economists/index.en.md
#: content/seeds/the-priorities/index.en.md
#: content/seeds/the-reservists/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Raw Research Notes"
msgstr "Unbearbeitete Recherchenotizen"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-non-economists/index.en.md
msgid "What we have then - whether in terms of Carbon Credits, LCAs or other aspects - is a question how to structure a system to make sense and be unhackable."
msgstr "Was wir haben werden – ob als Carbon Credits, LCAs oder etwas anderes – ist die Herausforderung ein System so zu strukturieren, dass es Sinn ergibt und nicht ausgetrickst werden kann."

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-non-economists/index.en.md
msgid "One solution would be maximum transparency and treating the whole LCA process: the knowledge base, algorithms, specific decisions as a wiki, where everybody can look into and comment. How much can we offload on citizen scientists and citizen economists, however?"
msgstr "Eine Möglichkeit wäre maximale Transparenz und den ganzen Lebenszyklus als LCA-Prozess: Das Wissen, die Daten, die Algorithmen, und spezielle Entscheidungen als Wiki, wo jeder reinschauen und kommentieren kann. Aber wie viel können wir an Laienwissenschafler:innen und Ökonomie-Amateur:innen abgeben?"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-non-economists/index.en.md
msgid "This will also lead to faction wars, both in terms of ideology and economics. Every decision will have consequences - and even without layers of red tape and sleazy CEOs people can be rallied to vote against something important. What if the calculations show that - for example - India should not produce steel, which could be picked up by another, much smaller country? The sheer population and number of votes can out-weight it! Will they then vote on a flawed calculation method, led by a demagogue?"
msgstr "Das wird auch zu Fraktionskämpfe führen, sowohl in ideologischer als auch ökonomischer Hinsicht. Jede Entscheidung wird Konsequenzen haben -- auch ohne überbordende Bürokratie und schmierige CEOs können Leute dazu gebracht werden, gegen etwas wichtiges zu steimmen. Was wenn die Berechnungen beispielsweise zeigen, dass Indien keinen Stahl produzieren sollte, sondern ein ein anderes, viel kleineres Land? Die Schiere Anzahl an Wähler:innen könnte die Rechnungen überstimmen! Werden sie dann für eine andere, fehlerbehaftete Berechnungsmethode stimmen, angeleitet von einer Demagogin?"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-non-economists/index.en.md
msgid "The bribes don't need to be financial. They can be prestige, acceptance by a faction, or whatever else."
msgstr "Die Erpressung muss nicht finanzieller Natur sein. Es könnte Prestige sein, Annahme bei einer Fraktion oder was auch immer."

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-non-economists/index.en.md
msgid "This prompt ties in with [the Miners](/seeds/the-miners), [The Moonshot](/seeds/the-moonshot) and many others."
msgstr "Diese Gedanken fügen sich mit [den Mienenarbeiter:innen](/de/seeds/the-miners), [der Mondmission](/de/seeds/the-moonshot) und vielen anderen ein."

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-non-economists/index.en.md
msgid "Let's look for a story in it though:"
msgstr "Aber lasst uns nach einer Geschichte suchen:"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-non-economists/index.en.md
msgid "Let's imagine a group of LCA scientists who just published just another analysis, being abruptly woken by their notification inboxes exploding. They were just launched on the front lines of a faction war, where their report was the \"last straw\" and might now contribute do a huge societal change, removing whole sectors of economy from one region of the world into another. Do they trust their work? Will they buckle under pressure? It's a good opportunity to walk the reader through how the LCA process looks like."
msgstr "Man stelle sich vor, eine Gruppe von LCA-Forscher:innen, die gerade erst eine weitere Analyse publiziert hat, wird abrupt von ihren Benachrichtigungen geweckt. Verschickt wurden die Nachrichten von den Frontlinien eines Fraktionskrieges, wo ihr Bericht der letzte Tropen war, der das Fass zum Überlaufen gebracht hat, und vielleicht einen großen gesellschaftlichen Wandel losgetreten hat, der ganze Sektoren der Wirtschaft von einer Region der Welt in eine andere verlegt. Werden Sie ihrer Arbeit trauen? Werden sie unter dem Druck nachgeben? Es ist eine gute Möglichkeit zu zeigen, wie ein LCA-Prozess aussieht."

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-non-economists/index.en.md
msgid "Consider the world to be more anarchist, less hierarchical, where a lot of decisions are consensus-based and a subject of public debate, flames and online brigading. The scientists behind this report are now celebrities, widely known, whether they want it or not. If you want to cite a book with similar themes, you can go with LX Beckett's \"Gamechanger\" or \"Dealbreaker\", where the popular support for eco-policies is one of the most important plots of both novels."
msgstr "Jetzt nehmen wir mal an, die Welt wäre mehr anarchistisch, weniger hierarchisch, und eine Menge Entscheidungen werden per Konsens entschieden, als öffentliche Debatte, Flaming oder Online Brigading. Die Wissenschaftler:innen hinter diesem Bericht sind jetzt berühmt, allseits bekannt, ob sie wollen oder nicht. Wenn man ein Buch mit ähnlichen Themen nennen will, könnte man LX Becketts „Gamechanger“ oder „Dealbreaker“ erwähnen, wo die populäre Unterstützung für grüne Politik eine der wichtigsten Themen der Handlung ist."

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-non-economists/index.en.md
msgid "Let's remember that more and more LCA processes are not just about energy and material, but are trying to count-in the uncountable, the effects on human happiness and labour practices. Yes, we could move the industry to China, but the general economic effect will produce X more tons of CO2, even if the factories will be more efficient."
msgstr "Lasst uns nicht vergessen, dass es bei mehr LCA-Prozesse nicht nur über mehr Energie und Materialien geht, sonder darum das mitzubrechnen, das nicht mit Zahlen versehen werden kann, die Auswirkungen auf menschliches Glück und Arbeitsbedingungen. Ja, wir könnten die Industrie nach China verlegen, aber die generellen ökonomischen Auswirkungen werden X Tonnen mehr CO2 verursachen, sogar wenn die Fabriken effizienter werden."

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-non-economists/index.en.md
#: content/seeds/the-priorities/index.en.md
msgid "Original notes:"
msgstr "Ursprüngliche Notizen:"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-non-economists/index.en.md
msgid "If they aren’t careful, they could become like the economists of the past centuries, worshiping a mathematical model and a paradigm, instead of continuously testing it."
msgstr "Wenn sie nicht vorsichtig sind, könnten sie wie die Ökonom:innen der letzten Jahrhunderte werden, mathematische Modell und Paradigmen anbeten, anstellen diese stetig zu überprüfen."

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-non-economists/index.en.md
msgid "Struggles of morality are ongoing in solarpunk"
msgstr "Der Kampf um Moralität ist im Gange"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-non-economists/index.en.md
#: content/seeds/the-priorities/index.en.md
msgid "Sources:"
msgstr "Quellen:"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-non-economists/index.en.md
msgid "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Life-cycle_assessment"
msgstr "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Life-cycle_assessment"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-non-economists/index.en.md
msgid "We can throw in the https://globalcarbonreward.org/ and let's say, \"good faith\", non-blockchain carbon counting systems. We WILL need one."
msgstr "Wir können https://globalcarbonreward.org/ mit dazu packen, quasi in „Treu und Glauben“, als CO2-Zählsystem ohne Blockchain. Wir WERDEN eins brauchen."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/seeds/the-pharmacists/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Pharmacists"
msgstr "Die Apotheker:innen"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-pharmacists/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "> A motley collection of neo-archeologists, data experts, doctors and biohackers are going through databases of the fallen pharmaceutical corporations, looking for drugs and solutions which worked, but were too cheap for the company giants to market. With so many medicines and procedures gone or extremely hard to get, maybe this is the best chance to rediscover cures?\n"
msgstr "> Eine bunte Gruppe aus Neo-Archeolog:innen, Datenexpert:innen, Ärztinnen und Biohacker durchsuchen die Datenbanken von gefallenen Pharmakonzernen, auf der Suche nach Medikamenten und Lösungen, die funktioniert haben, aber zu billig für die Marktgiganten waren. Mit so viel Medikamenten und Eingriffen, die weggefallen, oder schwer zu bekommen sind, ist das vielleicht die beste Chance, um Heilmethoden wiederzuentdecken?\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-pharmacists/index.en.md
msgid "[Solarpunk Prompts Podcast Episode](https://podcast.tomasino.org/@SolarpunkPrompts/episodes/the-pharmacists)"
msgstr "[Solarpunk Prompts Podcast Episode](https://podcast.tomasino.org/@SolarpunkPrompts/episodes/the-pharmacists)"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-pharmacists/index.en.md
msgid "[Transcript](https://wiki.tomasino.org/writing/Solarpunk-Prompts---The-Pharmacists)"
msgstr "[Transkription](https://wiki.tomasino.org/writing/Solarpunk-Prompts---The-Pharmacists)"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/seeds/the-priorities/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Priorities"
msgstr "Die Prioritäten"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-priorities/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "> A team of architects and civil engineers working on future-proofing their community need to make a hard decision. They are trying to prioritize the threats, but it’s a gamble trying to balance effectiveness and accessibility. They could make sure that one block won’t get flooded, but another district would need to wait.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-priorities/index.en.md
msgid "Continuing the architecture and infrastructure again, this time from the perspective of the architects. This can be a pre-solarpunk or solarpunk endeavor, shown as more reactionary in the chaos of everything, or more of a \"good practice\" after decades of notes and hard decisions already made."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-priorities/index.en.md
msgid "This is NOT a crisis response team. The flood, the heatwave, the hurricane are not here yet. You are to make them less threatening, not start evacuating people right now."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-priorities/index.en.md
msgid "The \"accessibility\" means three things: access of an average citizen to the infrastructure (a shelter maybe?), access of poorer / less fortunate residents to protenctions in their district, and of course access of the disabled citizens to things they need, as wheelchair-bound people will really struggle with knee-high floods."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-priorities/index.en.md
msgid "Will this mean abandoning districts and forcible relocations, or worse, climate ghettos?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-priorities/index.en.md
msgid "Assuming the team has access to all the required data, scientists, meteorologists, city archives: how many different kinds of climate threats can they protect us from? What will help with heatwaves, what with floods, hurricanes?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-priorities/index.en.md
msgid "What prices are considered too steep to pay? Are we going to surrender historical sites, places of remembrance? Are we okay with destroying a flood shaft and flooding a nature reserve to protect the population?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-priorities/index.en.md
msgid "How does the background of the team members play into that? Who already lives in a \"safe\", sutstainable tower, radiating pride and confidence, who clings to their family house in the suburbs, who cannot afford leaving a dangerous building which will not survive the next cataclysm?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-priorities/index.en.md
msgid "What time-scale are we talking about? Are we okay with cheaper protections that will last a year, are we going for 5 years, a decade, or more?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-priorities/index.en.md
msgid "How do we communicate it to the population, not to appear as despots choosing one group over another?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-priorities/index.en.md
msgid "What if we fail, what if we prepared for a flood and an unexpected heatwave rolls over, killing thousands? How do team members deal with guilt, do they accept the blame? Deny it?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-priorities/index.en.md
msgid "A good book on the social infrastructure and the challenges of urban planning: https://www.goodreads.com/en/book/show/37707827 , with some tl;dr in https://99percentinvisible.org/episode/palaces-for-the-people/"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-priorities/index.en.md
msgid "https://reasonstobecheerful.world/waal-river-flooding-project/"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-priorities/index.en.md
msgid "https://www.preventionweb.net/news/germany-2021-floods-10-recommendations-resilience"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-priorities/index.en.md
msgid "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/features/2021-12-18/how-hamburg-learned-to-live-with-rising-water"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-priorities/index.en.md
msgid "https://www.archdaily.com/993434/can-architecture-and-urban-planning-fight-back-against-climate-change has some sources, but also a lot of \"fake\" solutions"
msgstr ""

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/seeds/the-refugee-camp/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Refugee Camp"
msgstr "Das Flüchtlingslager"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-refugee-camp/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "> There is a full-fledged town built from a refugee camp which was set up there two decades ago. The inhabitants speak their own creole, a mix of more than five languages, and have very shaky relationships with their neighboring communities or states, each of which considers it a lawless territory and might be plotting to take over.\n"
msgstr "> Hier gibt es eine ganze Stadt, die aus einem Flüchtlingslager erbaut wurde, das vor zwei Jahrzehnten hier entstanden war. Die Einwohner:innen sprechen ihr eigenes kreolisch, ein Mischmasch aus mehr als fünf Sprachen, und sie haben ziemlich wacklige Beziehungen zu ihren benachbarten Gemeinschaften oder Staaten, von denen alle die Stadt als gesetzloses Gebiet ansehen und vielleicht die Übernahme planen.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-refugee-camp/index.en.md
msgid "[Solarpunk Prompts Podcast Episode](https://podcast.tomasino.org/@SolarpunkPrompts/episodes/the-refugee-camp)"
msgstr "[Solarpunk Prompts Podcast Episode](https://podcast.tomasino.org/@SolarpunkPrompts/episodes/the-refugee-camp)"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-refugee-camp/index.en.md
msgid "[Transcript](https://wiki.tomasino.org/writing/Solarpunk-Prompts---The-Refugee-Camp)"
msgstr "[Transkription](https://wiki.tomasino.org/writing/Solarpunk-Prompts---The-Refugee-Camp)"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/seeds/the-reservists/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Reservists"
msgstr "Die Reservist:innen"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-reservists/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "> As a disaster strikes, completely overwhelming several communities, a group of friends is called back into service as first responders. Each of their lives took a different path since the Service, but as they scramble to remember their training - as flood control, epidemic trackers, trauma psychologists or radio technicians - they feel like one unit again. Meeting new kids, straight from the mandatory training everyone goes through - will they become their mentors, or struggle opening up to greenhorns?\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-reservists/index.en.md
msgid "There is A LOT of baggage coming with the idea of a military service, the indocrination of the military, nationalism, destroying the individualism, discriminating against queer people, hiding sexual abuse etc. Let's acknowledge that and instead of \"re-forging existing militaries\" (as is episode #11) let's focus on something else: life after service."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-reservists/index.en.md
msgid "Let's imagine that after finishing high school, but before going to the University, every person in our society goes through 2 years of training and climate service. It doesn't matter what gender they are, or if they are disabled: they get assigned to a specialization and they learn how to help their community and society in some way. They can be first responders, they can be electricians, logisticians, kindergardeners, forest rangers, flood experts od epidemic effort coordinators. They are not professionals - of course, they can align their careers along their training - but they are the \"service members\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-reservists/index.en.md
msgid "This gives people their first skillset, but at the same time assures that everyone in a given region can help in case of a catastrophe. In case of a given kind of help needed, people with the right expertise are called for, no matter where in life are they now - whether hairdressers, engineers or politicians."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-reservists/index.en.md
msgid "They were equal once, within their \"unit\", and they will be equal once more, standing at the flood embankments."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-reservists/index.en.md
msgid "What's important, this prompt is not set DURING their initial training and service (as per #11), but years after, when people are mobilized again."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-reservists/index.en.md
msgid "This gives us A LOT in terms of worldbuilding:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-reservists/index.en.md
msgid "Everyone has been through a similar experience. This gives them a friend-group for life, some more empathy for people from vastly different paths of life, but can also result in some tribalism."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#: content/seeds/the-reservists/index.en.md
msgid "Are there sports teams or political factions based on the \"service groups\"? The Firemen versus The Radio Guys?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-reservists/index.en.md
msgid "Instead of being indoctrinated into patriotism and nationalism, our service members share a bond of saving lives and helping others in their own way. They might bring a lot of different and conflicting ideologies to the table, but this is something that connects them all."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-reservists/index.en.md
msgid "As with current military reservists, people will be called for trainings once every year, or several years. If they weren't a group of friends and a small community then, they probably will be."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-reservists/index.en.md
msgid "What in case of a drama? If Casey told Tom she really hates them, can they work well together under a lot of pressure, during a cataclysm? There must be some procedures in place for that!"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-reservists/index.en.md
msgid "Will they naturally navigate to live close together, potentially making the whole social structure more fragile? The service members are supposed to be spread more-or-less uniformly in each region!"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-reservists/index.en.md
msgid "In our Solarpunk world we want to imagine full transparency, so no \"buying easier spots\" in a team. Everyone gets a specialization along their skills and limitations and everyone is equal."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-reservists/index.en.md
msgid "How does a mobilization look like? What if someone is sick, pregnant, or cannot leave their position - for example at the power plant?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/seeds/the-reservists/index.en.md
msgid "From a very human side: how does mobilization look like? Is it a thrill, \"me and my friends are going to save some asses?\""
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-reservists/index.en.md
msgid "While there might be a lot to explain in this prompt, I think the story itself would be really fun and enjoyable both to write and read. The action, the dramatism is right there, and it's full of potential \"flashbacks\" to regular lives in a Solarpunk world."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/seeds/the-reservists/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Service Members vs Volunteers"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-reservists/index.en.md
msgid "The focus on this prompt can go both ways and I think both are equally interesting. The first is the mandated Service that a lot of people might not like, as it's \"too authoritarian\", while the latter is just Volunteering, which assumes that people got the necessary training on their own (like https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Icelandic_Association_for_Search_and_Rescue or Volunteer Firefighters)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-reservists/index.en.md
msgid "The very heart of the prompt is people who are leading normal lives until they are called for help - and their social dynamics, since it's what creates the story. Emphasizing how volunteering works right now could help the listeners imagine that, but I also think that imagining a huge cultural shift where everybody shares this experience is important."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/seeds/the-reservists/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Generational Shift"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-reservists/index.en.md
msgid "An interesting aspect of the story would be the first year / generation of the Reservists and how alien, oppressive the program might feel - set against the culture 20+ years later, where it's normalized, and everyone shares the duty / responsibility of the Service."
msgstr ""

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/seeds/the-ship/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Ship"
msgstr "Das Schiff"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/seeds/the-ship/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "> There is a modern cargo ship made with sails and solar panels, trying to replace the oil guzzlers of old and connect the world again. It is crewed by sailors old and young, engineers maintaining some experimental solutions, and some communities trying to travel in old container-houses. They have a lot on their plate.\n"
msgstr "> Es gibt ein modernes Frachtschiff mit Segeln und Solarpanels, das versucht die alten sprittfressenden Containerschiffe zu ersetzen und die Welt wieder zu verbinden. Die Besatzung besteht aus alten und jungen Segler:innen, Ingenieur:innen um die experimentellen Lösungen zu warten, und einige Gemeinschaften, die in ihren alten Containerhäusern verreisen. Sie haben viel zu tun.\n"

